+# S5-CLM-00003613 process audit
+
+The target-local process follows INTAKE → STATEMENT → ANCHOR → TREE → MACHINE → READABLE → VALIDATE → RELEASE. The immutable workset record, source locator, declaration/type digests, provider revision, and Stage6 alias are copied into the intake and crosswalk records. The pinned provider file is used only as statement provenance; no source proof body or `sorryAx` is accepted as proof authority.
+
+The three Lean surfaces use `import Mathlib` and retain the exact numeric provider module and qualified declaration in provenance comments. They contain no placeholder, unsafe injection, local semantic definition, notation, macro, alias, or import substitution. The semantic environment records the root-expression lock, transitive provider bindings, bidirectional transport, cold replay, and mutation obligations. The canonical Master must independently recompute elaboration and trust-zero closure after harvest.
+
+The readable DAG has four required nodes with exact forward and reverse anchors. Its hypotheses, inference, outputs, formal anchors, downstream uses, exceptional cases, and trust boundaries are retained in structured evidence. Release is provisional until the Master accepts the handoff.
