+# Full study: Erdős 1048, `r ≤ 1` variant
+
+The frozen statement concerns a monic complex polynomial of positive degree whose roots lie in the closed disk of radius `r`, with `0 < r ≤ 1`. It asserts the existence of a point in the open level set whose connected component has extended diameter larger than `ENNReal.ofReal (2 - r)`.
+
+The study records the exact source declaration, type, docstring context, locator, provider revision, and Stage6 alias. The formal target is kept structurally unchanged: all seven hypotheses and the existential conclusion remain present. The proof-unit DAG separates statement identification, semantic transport, machine audit, and readable reconstruction. Exceptional cases and trust boundaries are retained in each node record; generated prose is not used as proof authority.
+
+The source repository theorem is marked `sorryAx` in the pinned statement provider. Accordingly, this package does not treat that body as a proof. It supplies an independent claim-owned Lean surface and leaves canonical trust-zero recompilation and semantic substitution replay to Master.
